SUMMARY:Black Family Day
DESCRIPTION:Join us for Black Family Day 2026 — a celebration of Black culture\, community\, and excellence bringing together students\, alumni\, families\, and community members. \n📍 UC Davis Quad\n📅 Saturday\, May 23\, 2026\n⏰ 12 PM – 8 PM \n🌟 Theme: Built to Last: Black Strength Through Time \nSince 1970\, Black Family Day has been a cornerstone at UC Davis — fostering joy\, connection\, and unity through the celebration of Black culture and heritage. \n🎊 Enjoy food vendors\, craft booths\, family activities\, a mechanical bull\, live performances\, DJs\, dancers\, poets\, alumni wine & jazz\, and more! \n🎶 Featuring Bino Rideaux (Los Angeles) \nAlso featuring DJ KweKu\, Ladies of Davis\, Afro Vibes\, Honey Steppers\, The NME Band\, and more. \n🎁 RSVP HERE for Drawings\n🎷 Alumni Wine & Jazz\n🌐 Click HERE for our Website \n⭐ Come celebrate culture\, honor legacy\, and uplift community — because our legacy is Built to Last.
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/black-family-day/
LOCATION:UC Davis Quad
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Black-Family-Day-2026.jpg
